.TH ED25519TEST 1
.SH NAME
ed25519test \- test Ed25519 signature verification
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ed25519test
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Ed25519test
checks
.IR ed25519 (2)
against RFC 8032's own published test vectors (\c
.BR "section 7.1" ),
the standard's actual key/message/signature values, offline:
.IP \(bu
each vector's genuine signature must verify;
.IP \(bu
the same signature with one bit flipped must
.I not
verify; nor must the signature against a one-bit-changed message, nor
under a one-bit-changed public key \(em automated negative controls (a
wrong verification is a safe computation, so unlike most controls in
this tree it can be automated).
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/cmd/ed25519test.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR ed25519 (2),
.IR p256test (1)
.SH BUGS
Coverage is verification over the two fixed vectors plus the bit-flip
controls;
.IR ed25519 (2)
does not sign, so there is nothing to round-trip.
